    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“Traitors are vermin, Ara,” he says, tauntingly. “They breed. Who knows how many people Dezeeves has been whispering to?",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6024
        }
      ],
      "words": 41
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I can’t make him directly kill himself, I remember. But, maybe",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6759
        },
        {
          "text": "In my mind’s eye, I can even see him. He’s smirking, standing by a telescope in The Bridge of a hive which is travelling",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6822
        }
      ],
      "words": 75
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“What did he say?” he asks me, with love in his eyes. And I turn cold as granite. I take his hand, shakily, knowing I wi",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7498
        }
      ],
      "words": 63
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“You can block my magic, Drake. But you can’t stop my choices.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9594
        }
      ],
      "words": 12
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Dezeeves’ words penetrate a hole through any hope I had left. Of me. Of Cosmer. Of the future we should have, but can’t.",
